{"availability":"available","full":"aurelia/ui-virtualization","name":"ui-virtualization","description":"A plugin that provides a virtualized repeater and other virtualization services.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":89,"forks":44,"created":"2015-06-27T03:23:52Z","updated":"2023-03-15T00:05:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://aurelia-ui-virtualization.now.sh/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:36.408Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:36.408Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:36.408Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:18.945Z","stars":89,"forks":44},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:36.408Z","stars":89,"forks":44}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This library is part of the Aurelia platform and contains a plugin that provides a virtualized repeater and other virtualization services. This plugin enables \"virtualization\" of list through a new virtual-repeat.for. When used, the list \"virtually\" as tens or hundreds of thousands of rows, but the DOM only actually has rows for what is visible. It could be only tens of items. This allows rendering of massive lists of data with amazing performance. It works like repeat.for, it just creates a scrolling area and manages the list using UI virtualization techniques.","To keep up to date on Aurelia, please visit and subscribe to the official blog and our email list. We also invite you to follow us on twitter. If you have questions look around our Discourse forums, chat in our community on Discord or use stack overflow. Documentation can be found in our developer hub."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aurelia/ui-virtualization/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"65cb4d56a3942e89eea5b87e1d82acf587f30d22729e161e72fdb7f9b817f068","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:27:06.997Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.606Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-03-15T00:05:35Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.608Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This library is part of the Aurelia platform and contains a plugin that provides a virtualized repeater and other virtualization services. This plugin enables \"virtualization\" of list through a new virtual-repeat.for. When used, the list \"virtually\" as tens or hundreds of thousands of rows, but the DOM only actually has rows for what is visible. It could be only tens of items. This allows rendering of massive lists of data with amazing performance. It works like repeat.for, it just creates a scrolling area and manages the list using UI virtualization techniques.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aurelia/ui-virtualization/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"65cb4d56a3942e89eea5b87e1d82acf587f30d22729e161e72fdb7f9b817f068","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aurelia/ui-virtualization/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.606Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aurelia/ui-virtualization/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T18:44:57.787Z","hash":"65cb4d56a3942e89eea5b87e1d82acf587f30d22729e161e72fdb7f9b817f068","originalBytes":8106,"storedBytes":8106,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["item","html","index","plugin","items","list","npm","virtualization","aurelia","build","javascript","run","code","export","install","repeat","used","around","aurelia-ui-virtualization","bar","baz","class","controllers","css","element","example","foo","height","like","myvirtuallist","other","overflow","platform","rows","scroll","shell","similar","template","tests","virtual-repeat","work","appropriate","cannot","chat","command","discord","discourse","dom","ensure","folder","follow","following","getmore","inserting","let","library","load","nth-child","only","order","project","provides","removing","repeated","requires","running","selector","steps","tens","their","these","twitter","view","virtual","visible",